 ## Subtopics
 
 ### MetaNLR Baseline
-MetaNLR is a variant of NLR that wraps the NLR implementation with an outer meta-learning loop using the Reptile algorithm [S1, unofficial]. It learns the initialization of the shape and color networks to enable rapid specialization to new test scenes using only a few inner-loop steps [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when few-shot novel view synthesis is required [S1, unofficial]. The meta-learning rate is set to $5 \times 10^{-2}$ [S1, unofficial]. It uses the same training and testing views at 800x600 resolution as the baseline NLR [S1, unofficial].
+MetaNLR is a variant that wraps the NLR implementation with an outer meta-learning loop using Reptile [S1, unofficial]. It learns the initialization of the shape and color networks to enable rapid specialization to new scenes. It is chosen when few-shot novel view synthesis is required. It uses a meta-learning rate of $5 \times 10^{-2}$ [S1, unofficial]. Unlike the baseline, it performs meta-training and meta-testing on the same scenes, specializing via inner-loop updates on training/testing views at 800x600 resolution [S1, unofficial].
 
